=com.google.oauth-client:google-oauth-client:1.35.0 '--agent-command=claude -p --permission-mode bypassPermissions --model sonnet'\n\n\nWelcome to Gradle 9.1.0!\n\nHere are the highlights of this release:\n - Full Java 25 support\n - Native task graph visualization\n - Enhanced console output\n\nFor more details see https://docs.gradle.org/9.1.0/release-notes.html\n\nTo honour the JVM settings for this build a single-use Daemon process will be forked. For more on this, please refer to https://docs.gradle.org/9.1.0/userguide/gradle_daemon.html#sec:disabling_the_daemon in the Gradle documentation.\nDaemon will be stopped at the end of the build \nShared read-only dependency cache is an incubating feature.\n> Task :tck-build-logic:extractPluginRequests UP-TO-DATE\n> Task :tck-build-logic:generatePluginAdapters UP-TO-DATE\n> Task :tck-build-logic:compileJava UP-TO-DATE\n> Task :tck-build-logic:compileGroovy UP-TO-DATE\n> Task :tck-build-logic:compileGroovyPlugins UP-TO-DATE\n> Task :tck-build-logic:pluginDescriptors UP-TO-DATE\n> Task :tck-build-logic:processResources UP-TO-DATE\n> Task :tck-build-logic:classes UP-TO-DATE\n> Task :tck-build-logic:jar UP-TO-DATE\n\n> Configure project :\nGraalVM Reachability Metadata TCK\n---------------------------------\n\n> Task :discoverArtifactMetadata\nI've populated the metadata file with all discovered fields, confirmed against Maven Central and GitHub.\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| repository-url | `https://github.com/googleapis/google-oauth-java-client` |\n| source-code-url | Maven Central sources jar (`$version$`) |\n| test-code-url | Maven Central tests jar (`$version$`) |\n| documentation-url | Maven Central javadoc jar (`$version$`) |\n| language | absent (plain Java, not language-specific) |\n| not-for-native-image | absent (it's a standard JVM jar with real class files) |\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- I checked the sibling `com.google.http-client:google-http-client` entry already in this repo's `metadata/` tree first, since it's published by the same GitHub org (googleapis) with a nearly identical build setup. That entry already preferred Maven Central's `-sources.jar`/`-tests.jar`/`-javadoc.jar` URLs over GitHub tag links — matching the task's explicit preference for Maven-hosted artifacts when available — so I mirrored that exact pattern rather than inventing a new convention.\n- I verified each of the three Maven Central URLs with `curl -I` (HTTP 200) and listed the directory before trusting them, rather than constructing them from the version number and assuming they'd resolve — Maven Central doesn't always publish a `-tests.jar` for every artifact, so this check matters.\n- `google-oauth-client` is a pure-Java artifact with no Android/JS/native-specific variant, so neither \"language\" nor \"not-for-native-image\" applies — unlike, say, a Kotlin or Android-only AAR artifact where those fields would be required.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\nRan agent for com.google.oauth-client:google-oauth-client:1.35.0 (exit 0). Log: /home/mihailo/git/graalvm-reachability-metadata/forge/local_repositories/forge_worktrees/10701-c0bc26b5/build/agent-artifact-discovery-logs/com.google.oauth-client-google-oauth-client-1.35.0.log\n\n[Incubating] Problems report is available at: file:///home/mihailo/git/graalvm-reachability-metadata/forge/local_repositories/forge_worktrees/10701-c0bc26b5/build/reports/problems/problems-report.html\n\nDeprecated Gradle features were used in this build, making it incompatible with Gradle 10.\n\nYou can use '--warning-mode all' to show the individual deprecation warnings and determine if they come from your own scripts or plugins.\n\nFor more on this, please refer to https://docs.gradle.org/9.1.0/userguide/command_line_interface.html#sec:command_line_warnings in the Gradle documentation.\n\nBUILD SUCCESSFUL in 1m 55s\n9 actionable tasks: 1 executed, 8 up-to-date\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1791894341049}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_OEpa8UytTMOwQ8v9XUNycBmC|fc_0fb330794fc073b2016ace23441c0c87d194a01e07cbb2f720", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe key fact that resolves this: `com.google.api.client.testing.http.MockHttpTransport` — used by the recently generated `google-api-services-sqladmin` test to mock HTTP responses without a live network call — ships *inside* the main `google-http-client` jar itself, not a separate `google-http-client-test` artifact. Since `google-oauth-client` already pulls `google-http-client` in as a compile dependency, the generated scaffold gets OAuth-flow HTTP mocking for free, with zero extra Maven coordinates.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nFindings from research:\n- **POM (1.35.0)**: compile deps are `google-http-client`, `google-http-client-gson`, and `guava` — all pure-Java, already well-represented elsewhere in this metadata repo with no special setup.\n- **Contrast case**: `com.google.auth:google-auth-library-oauth2-http` (a *different* library, despite the similar name) needed an extra `com.google.appengine:appengine-api-1.0-sdk` test dependency because it has real App Engine classes. `google-oauth-client`'s jar contents show no such AppEngine/servlet coupling — just `oauth2`, `oauth` (1.0a signing), and `openidconnect` packages.\n- **Crypto**: `OAuthHmacSigner`/`OAuthRsaSigner` use standard `javax.crypto`/`java.security` JCA primitives (HMAC-SHA1/256, RSA) — no custom provider or keystore needed under Native Image.\n- **No network/Docker need**: OAuth flow tests (`AuthorizationCodeFlow`, `Credential`, token exchange) can be fully exercised against a `MockHttpTransport` returning canned JSON token responses, exactly the pattern already used for `google-api-services-sqladmin`.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"no_action\",\n  \"summary\": \"Pure-Java OAuth helper library; compile deps (google-http-client, google-http-client-gson, guava) are already standard in this repo, and google-http-client transitively brings MockHttpTransport for mocking OAuth token exchanges without network/Docker. No AppEngine/servlet coupling (unlike the similarly-named google-auth-library-oauth2-http) and no special crypto/env setup needed for HMAC/RSA signing.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Use com.google.api.client.testing.http.MockHttpTransport/MockLowLevelHttpResponse (bundled in google-http-client, already a transitive dependency) to stub token-endpoint responses when testing AuthorizationCodeFlow/TokenRequest/Credential instead of hitting a live OAuth endpoint.\",\n  \"risks\": []\n}\n```\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1791894341053}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_7M0n7tdqiaVZoTCvodKMlkmM|fc_0fb330794fc073b2016ace23441c1087d18e6d7ede40d8c622", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Prompt:\nYou are preparing a Forge workflow for a library issue. Decide whether the library needs setup beyond the normal generated test scaffold before meaningful coverage is reachable.\n\nResearch the library yourself to make this decision. Investigate the resolved artifact and its dependencies, how the library is normally used, and its documentation. The JSON context below is only a starting point, not the limit of what you may consider. Do not modify the repository or apply any setup yourself — return only the decision. Local Gradle and Native Image verification remain authoritative.\n\nThe setup can be one of three things: an extra Maven dependency, a Docker image the tests need, or an environment/system property the generated tests must set. Represent dependencies and Docker images as `deterministic_setup` entries the driver can apply before generation:\n  - {\"kind\": \"dependency\", \"coordinate\": \"group:artifact:version\", \"scope\": \"testImplementation\", \"reason\": \"...\"}\n  - {\"kind\": \"docker_image\", \"image\": \"name:tag\", \"slug\":